# QA replay of the update band and its cue, UPDATE READY (owner, 2026-10-15: "A Beta-tester did not realize there is an
# update, which shows me that it is currently too subtle. I, however, do not want to have a blocking modal like a
# pop-up"; from a panel of four: B, "A cue, then the band"). A developer build plays it with --dev-view --dev-script;
# how to run it, and what each still must show: update-ready.md beside this file. Times are in seconds.
#
# A snapshot step takes about 0.5 to 1 s (the developer view's tabs follow while the script goes on; until 2026-10-26
# they were in the step, about 1.6 s then) and the step after it follows 0.3 s later, so the waits below are what is
# left between the stills, not their moments: update-ready.md has those.

# A --dev-view session starts on settings of its own, as at a first start, so the tour opened by itself at chapter 1
# once the data was there. It ends first.
tour end
# Customs' artwork read once, so the raid below has its map at once.
map customs
wait 3

# The next patch of this version taken for downloaded, in the menus, as a download that just completed leaves it: the
# band under MAP glows in, and the cue comes once the map's middle has been free 0.5 s.
trigger update
wait 0.5
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\update-ready\t0
# The cue whole and still, its title decoded (from 1.6 s).
wait 1.4
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\update-ready\t1
# The cue fades from 4.4 s; from 4.6 s the band glows again, for 1.2 s; the still comes after that.
wait 3.7
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\update-ready\t2

# A PMC raid on Customs: the band goes as the raid loads, and the raid card's head holds its row.
load
steps
start
wait 3
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\update-ready\t3

# The raid ends: RAID OVER for 5 s (no positions, so no replay), the band back with its glow; then the cue once more.
end
wait 9
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\update-ready\t4
exit
